---
title: Gaviidae
---
# Gaviidae

Gaviidae holds the loons, heavy-bodied northern waterbirds with a dagger bill.
They take perch and eels by descending from the surface and propelling
themselves through the water after them, driven by the feet, and routinely stay
submerged for a minute at depths of several metres. The eye focuses in air and
below the surface alike through a deformable lens, so a descending loon does not
lose sight of its prey. See [[common-loon]].
